  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia - Malaria - Zambia (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia, Malaria, Churches Health Association of Zambia (CHAZ)This program has the following goals: Establish and maintain 5  malaria-free districts  in Zambia by 2016.  Reduce malaria deaths to near zero and reduce all-cause child mortality by 20% by 2016.  Reduce malaria incidence by 75% of the 2010 baseline by 2016. The objectives of this program are: To ensure that all prioritized operations research to generate evidence to support informed decision-making on policy and implementation of malaria programme and iCCM By 2016.  To have 100% of households and persons at risk in targeted areas have access to evidence-based vector control and other preventive interventions by 2016.  To have, 100% of suspected-malaria cases in all health facilities receive parasitological confirmation (microscopy or RDT) and 100% of the confirmed cases at facility and community levels receive prompt and appropriate treatment, including treatment of under-five pneumonia and diarrhoea, as detailed in national diagnosis and treatment guidelines by 2016..  To improve capacity in coordination, leadership, governance and resource mobilization for effective and efficient management of the NMCP.  To increase knowledge levels of malaria to 100% and improve uptake and correct use of interventions to 80% by 2016.  To strengthen surveillance, M&amp;E systems in order to ensure timely availability of quality, consistent and relevant data on Malaria control performance by 2016</narrative>
  </description>
